            <ArticleTitle>[Jejunal diverticulitis. A rare cause of acute abdomen].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>357-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Non-Meckelian jejunoileal diverticula are more frequently diagnosed in men aged more than 50 years old. They are a rare cause of acute abdomen. They are usually asymptomatic and are estimated to cause complications in 10-20% of cases. We present the recently diagnosed case of an 82-year-old man admitted to our hospital.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
